{"acceptance_criteria":"","actor":"","agent_state":"","assignee":null,"await_id":"","await_type":"","close_reason":"Implemented in commit b7fef30 — see plan at ~/.claude/plans/enumerated-orbiting-boot.md","closed_at":"2026-04-11T01:03:13Z","closed_by_session":"","compacted_at":null,"compacted_at_commit":null,"compaction_level":0,"content_hash":"c4e3d5d7cbc03cc7f40ec5098e51f36520c2d61175c585435ced54861ef029a5","created_at":"2026-04-11T00:50:24Z","created_by":"Joshua Oliphant","crystallizes":0,"defer_until":null,"description":"Add a new 'brooklet watch \u003ctopic\u003e' CLI command that tails a brooklet topic and emits one compact human-readable line per event (e.g. '#42 14:03:22 type=ping n=10'), suitable for use with Claude Code's Monitor tool which turns each stdout line into a chat notification.\n\nRationale: brooklet's follow-mode consumer with offset tracking is a near-perfect fit for Monitor — resumable across restarts, no missed events, no replay. Existing 'consume --follow' emits raw JSON envelopes which would be too noisy for Monitor (it auto-kills verbose streams).\n\nPlan: /Users/joshuaoliphant/.claude/plans/enumerated-orbiting-boot.md\n\nScope:\n- New 'brooklet watch \u003ctopic\u003e' core CLI command (cli.py)\n- New pure formatter module src/brooklet/watch_format.py\n- Line-buffered stdout for pipe compatibility (sys.stdout.reconfigure)\n- Default group 'watch' for resumability\n- Tests: tests/test_watch_format.py (10 unit tests), tests/test_watch.py (CliRunner + 1 subprocess smoke test for real buffering)\n- TDD: tests first\n\nOut of scope: per-adapter scout/pytest formatters, --filter flag, fixing existing missing-file-in-follow-mode limitation.","design":"","due_at":null,"ephemeral":0,"estimated_minutes":null,"event_kind":"","external_ref":null,"hook_bead":"","id":"brooklet-3ot","is_template":0,"issue_type":"feature","last_activity":null,"metadata":"{}","mol_type":"","notes":"","original_size":null,"owner":"joshua.oliphant@hey.com","payload":"","pi