{"acceptance_criteria":"","actor":"","agent_state":"","assignee":null,"await_id":"","await_type":"","close_reason":"","closed_at":null,"closed_by_session":"","compacted_at":null,"compacted_at_commit":null,"compaction_level":0,"content_hash":"3c6b1b59062f4865bdd7f84eb49f4c4012096749de62474a9621562bb2abc002","created_at":"2026-03-24T05:05:14Z","created_by":"Joshua Oliphant","crystallizes":0,"defer_until":null,"description":"Create a brooklet plugin adapter for the ServiceNow work-tracker JSONL data at areas/ServiceNow/work-tracker/raw/. Monthly JSONL files contain commit and activity events with fields: type, timestamp, repo, branch, category, commit_type, enriched, impact, learnings, people. Plugin should register as brooklet work scan with analytics similar to scout/pytest pattern.","design":"","due_at":null,"ephemeral":0,"estimated_minutes":null,"event_kind":"","external_ref":null,"hook_bead":"","id":"brooklet-rvt","is_template":0,"issue_type":"feature","last_activity":null,"metadata":"{}","mol_type":"","notes":"","original_size":null,"owner":"joshua.oliphant@hey.com","payload":"","pinned":0,"priority":2,"quality_score":null,"rig":"","role_bead":"","role_type":"","sender":"","source_repo":"","source_system":"","spec_id":"","status":"open","target":"","timeout_ns":0,"title":"brooklet-work: work tracker analytics adapter","updated_at":"2026-03-24T05:05:14Z","waiters":"","wisp_type":"","work_type":""}
{"acceptance_criteria":"","actor":"","agent_state":"","assignee":null,"await_id":"","await_type":"","close_reason":"","closed_at":null,"closed_by_session":"","compacted_at":null,"compacted_at_commit":null,"compaction_level":0,"content_hash":"21f76b8d1badf81fa8a060dce9fd74b92778bbeae779181e9caa05cf7f332bb1","created_at":"2026-04-11T01:15:34Z","created_by":"Joshua Oliphant","crystallizes":0,"defer_until":null,"description":"Bug discovered while wiring 'brooklet watch' into Claude Code's Monitor tool.\n\nWhen 'produce()' auto-registers a local topic, the sources.json entry stores a path relative to the stream directory:\n\n  {\n    \"demo\": {\"path\": \"demo/data.jsonl\", \"mode\": \"single-file\"}\n  }\n\nBut when a consumer opens this path, it's resolved against the current working directory of the process — not against the --stream-dir. This breaks any scenario where brooklet is invoked with --stream-dir pointing somewhere other than the current cwd, which is exactly what happens when Monitor runs brooklet from the original shell's cwd.\n\nReproduction:\n\n  rm -rf /tmp/repro \u0026\u0026 mkdir /tmp/repro\n  echo '{\"a\":1}' | brooklet produce demo --stream-dir /tmp/repro\n  cd ~/some/other/project\n  brooklet watch demo --group test --stream-dir /tmp/repro\n  # UserWarning: Source file does not exist: demo/data.jsonl\n\nWorkaround: prefix invocations with 'cd \u003cstream-dir\u003e \u0026\u0026' so that cwd and stream-dir match.\n\nFix: in the Consumer (or earlier in Stream.consume), resolve relative paths from sources.json against the stream directory, not the cwd. Absolute paths from externally registered sources should still work as-is.\n\nAffects: all consumers, not just watch. Broken workflows include any script that runs brooklet from a different directory than where the stream lives.","design":"","due_at":null,"ephemeral":0,"estimated_minutes":null,"event_kind":"","external_ref":null,"hook_bead":"","id":"brooklet-uoj","is_template":0,"issue_type":"bug","last_activity":null,"metadata":"{}","mol_type":"","notes":"","original_size":null,"owner":"joshua.oliphant@hey.com","payload":"","pinned":0,"priority":2,"quality_score":null,"rig":"","role_bead":"","role_type":"","sender":"","source_repo":"","source_system":"","spec_id":"","status":"open","target":"","timeout_ns":0,"title":"Consumer: resolve registered source paths against --stream-dir, not cwd","updated_at":"2026-04-11T01:15:34Z","waiters":"","wisp_type":"","work_type":""}
